From 0890dbdd78c2db369d26971cb5f1f3eddf8ac78e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jetson <jetson@orin-nano.tail52323b.ts.net>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:42:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] nv_attach: map lookups take the key the program stored;
 definitions after .loc fail closed

An inline lookup (thread-local or sum map) whose key the program stored
into a stack slot just before, in the same basic block with nothing in
between that could write the slot or the stored register (a store the pass
cannot place in llvmbpf's frame, a call, an atomic, a label), takes the
stored register instead of loading the key back through the slot's generic
address. [%SP + o] and [%SPL + o] are the same bytes: %SP is cvta.local of
the depot (PTX ISA 6.4.1.1, cvta). Measured as a hand-written form on
lat_mmvq (proto/meas RULES-sum-map-build.md, passes h1/h2): 0.028-0.030 ns
per thread for its three lookups; the 1530 value through ld.local/st.local
(0.004) and 64-bit accesses (-0.002) did not show and are not built.

Review of 00f12354: a .loc directive (no ';') glued to the next statement
hid that statement's definitions, and /* */ comments were kept; both now
count (fail closed).

Tests [sum-map-routing]: forwarded forms (32/64-bit register, immediate),
and every case that must load again. pt_victim's five tools exact.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
